{{also|Singleton}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{suffix|single|ton|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|playing cards|lang=en}} A [[playing card]] that is the only one of its [[suit]] in a [[hand]], especially at [[bridge]].
# A [[single]] [[object]], especially one of a [[group]].
# {{context|computing|lang=en}} A [[class]] that may not be [[instantiate]]d more than once, i.e. that [[implement]]s the [[singleton pattern|singleton design pattern]].
# {{context|mathematics|lang=en}} A [[set]] with exactly one [[element]].
# A child or animal that is born singly, not as a [[twin]] or other multiple [[birth]].

